e at Ephrath, on the road between Bethel and Bethlehem, at a short distance from the latter place.","verses":157,"father":"Israel","mother":"Rachel","v":[12]}],"places":[{"id":"aphek_72","name":"Aphek","kind":"City","lat":32.10471,"lon":34.93198,"summary":"A city of the tribe of Issachar, near to Jezreel (1 Sam. 4:1; 29:1; comp. 28:4).","verses":3,"v":[1]},{"id":"ebenezer_350","name":"Ebenezer","kind":"","lat":31.83274,"lon":35.18016,"summary":"Stone of help, the memorial stone set up by Samuel to commemorate the divine assistance to Israel in their great battle against the Philistines, whom they totally routed (1 Sam. 7:7-12) at Aphek, in the neighbourhood of Mizpeh, in Benjamin, near the western entrance of the pass of Beth-horon.","verses":3,"v":[1]},{"id":"shiloh_1081","name":"Shiloh","kind":"City","lat":32.05617,"lon":35.28988,"summary":"Generally understood as denoting the Messiah, “the peaceful one,” as the word signifies (Gen. 49:10). The Vulgate Version translates the word, “he who is to be sent,” in allusion to the Messiah; the Revised Version, margin, “till he come to Shiloh;” and the LXX., “until that which is his shall come to Shiloh.”","verses":30,"v":[3,4,12]}],"events":[{"id":"death_of_eli_ark_captured_152","title":"Death of Eli, Ark Captured","year":-1122,"summary":"Passage: 1 Samuel 4:15–18. People: Eli.","v":[15,16,17,18]},{"id":"judgeship_of_eli_145","title":"Judgeship of Eli","year":-1162,"summary":"Passage: 1 Samuel 4:15–18. People: Eli. Place: Canaan. Lasted about 40 years.","v":[15,16,17,18]}],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[1697,1697,1697,8050,8050,1961,3605,3605,3478,3478,3478,3478,3318,3318,7122,7122,6430,6430,4421,4421,2583,2583,5921,72,6430,6430,6430,2583,663,663],[6430,6430,6186,6186,7122,3478,4421,4421,4421,4421,5203,3478,5062,5062,6440,6430,6430,5221,5221,5221,702,702,505,376,4634,4634,4634],[5971,5971,5971,935,413,4264,4264,2205,2205,3478,3478,559,4100,3068,3068,3068,5062,5062,5062,5062,6440,6430,643